{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-68b926e4-b574-4095-9925-fb373da445f0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-884b8c14dd5f4028","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9004-oz5mx3no/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9004-E001.md","content":"# Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers a complete disconnected-environment (air-gapped) installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The capability already exists and works in the product; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps — which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install — from private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs and is authored into the product documentation here, with technical review.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Author a disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode covering:\n  - Prerequisites for a disconnected cluster\n  - Operator configuration for raw deployment mode in an air-gapped environment (including which operators are not required in raw deployment mode)\n  - Post-install validation steps for verifying an air-gapped install\n- Include a complete image-mirroring reference: the required images and how to derive the digest list per release\n- Add a troubleshooting section covering the three most common field-reported failure modes:\n  - Image pull errors\n  - Missing runtime\n  - Storage-initializer misconfiguration\n- Technically review all published content for accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no Service Mesh/serverless dependency; InferenceService CRs; dependency on Serving Runtimes for model execution)\n- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes; serverless mode disconnected support is out of scope\n\n### Content outline\n\n1. **Prerequisites** — disconnected cluster requirements; mirrored container registry access; KServe raw deployment mode as the recommended disconnected path\n2. **Operator configuration** — required operator configuration for raw deployment mode; operators that can be skipped in a disconnected raw-deployment install\n3. **Image mirroring reference** — required images list; procedure to derive the image digest list per release\n4. **Installation validation** — steps to verify the air-gapped install (InferenceService readiness, predictor readiness)\n5. **Troubleshooting** — image pull errors; missing runtime; storage-initializer misconfiguration\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps\n- The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference listing the required images and describing how to derive the digest list per release\n- The troubleshooting section covers image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration\n- All technical content is validated for accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode behavior, operator requirements, image and runtime dependencies); the review is performed by the owning serving team and any discrepancies are corrected before publication\n- Content follows the Red Hat docs content process (builds and renders in the docs toolchain)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): Disconnected install guide covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps — fully covered by this epic\n- HLR-2 (P1): Complete image-mirroring reference — fully covered by this epic\n- HLR-3 (P2): Troubleshooting section for the three most common field-reported failure modes — fully covered by this epic\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input