{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86c35386040d6756","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9004-E001\n3\ttitle: Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9004\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Disconnected environment install guide for KServe raw deployment mode\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a complete disconnected-environment (air-gapped) installation guide for KServe raw deployment mode in the product documentation. The capability already exists and works in the product; the gap is entirely published guidance. Field teams currently rediscover the required steps — which images to mirror, which operators to skip, how to verify an air-gapped install — from private gists. Source material exists in field enablement docs and is authored into the product documentation here, with technical review.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Author a disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode covering:\n38\t  - Prerequisites for a disconnected cluster\n39\t  - Operator configuration for raw deployment mode in an air-gapped environment (including which operators are not required in raw deployment mode)\n40\t  - Post-install validation steps for verifying an air-gapped install\n41\t- Include a complete image-mirroring reference: the required images and how to derive the digest list per release\n42\t- Add a troubleshooting section covering the three most common field-reported failure modes:\n43\t  - Image pull errors\n44\t  - Missing runtime\n45\t  - Storage-initializer misconfiguration\n46\t- Technically review all published content for accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode uses plain Deployments/Services with no Service Mesh/serverless dependency; InferenceService CRs; dependency on Serving Runtimes for model execution)\n47\t- No code, operator, or default-configuration changes; serverless mode disconnected support is out of scope\n48\t\n49\t### Content outline\n50\t\n51\t1. **Prerequisites** — disconnected cluster requirements; mirrored container registry access; KServe raw deployment mode as the recommended disconnected path\n52\t2. **Operator configuration** — required operator configuration for raw deployment mode; operators that can be skipped in a disconnected raw-deployment install\n53\t3. **Image mirroring reference** — required images list; procedure to derive the image digest list per release\n54\t4. **Installation validation** — steps to verify the air-gapped install (InferenceService readiness, predictor readiness)\n55\t5. **Troubleshooting** — image pull errors; missing runtime; storage-initializer misconfiguration\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- A disconnected install guide for KServe raw deployment mode is published in the product documentation, covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps\n60\t- The guide includes a complete image-mirroring reference listing the required images and describing how to derive the digest list per release\n61\t- The troubleshooting section covers image pull errors, missing runtime, and storage-initializer misconfiguration\n62\t- All technical content is validated for accuracy against the KServe architecture context (raw deployment mode behavior, operator requirements, image and runtime dependencies); the review is performed by the owning serving team and any discrepancies are corrected before publication\n63\t- Content follows the Red Hat docs content process (builds and renders in the docs toolchain)\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P1): Disconnected install guide covering prerequisites, operator configuration, and validation steps — fully covered by this epic\n68\t- HLR-2 (P1): Complete image-mirroring reference — fully covered by this epic\n69\t- HLR-3 (P2): Troubleshooting section for the three most common field-reported failure modes — fully covered by this epic\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83749fbced4ea679","agent_id":"ae64dd8cad651347f","session_id":"ca9abc0a-3749-41c9-8ee1-a3bd18ff525b","uuid":"b599de82-8d57-4053-ba5d-11110c1ac570","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:14:26.826Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86c35386040d6756","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9004 decomposition"}
